.\"
.\" SHMGET(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH SHMGET 2 "June 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
shmget \- get a System V shared memory segment identifier
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/ipc.h>
.B #include <sys/shm.h>
.PP
.BI "int shmget(key_t " key ", size_t " size ", int " shmflg ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR shmget ()
returns the identifier of the System V shared memory segment associated with
.IR key .
A new segment of at least
.I size
bytes (rounded up to a multiple of the page size) is created if
.I key
has the value
.B IPC_PRIVATE
or if no existing segment is associated with
.I key
and
.B IPC_CREAT
is set in
.IR shmflg .
.PP
The low 9 bits of
.I shmflg
define the permissions of the segment.  If
.B IPC_CREAT
and
.B IPC_EXCL
are both set then the call fails with
.B EEXIST
if a segment already exists for
.IR key .
.PP
On creation
.I size
must be at least
.B SHMMIN
(1) and not greater than
.BR SHMMAX .
The segment owns a run of physically contiguous pages, zero-filled at
creation, and shared by every process that
.BR shmat (2)\c
\&'s it.  For access to an existing segment
.I size
may be 0 (don't care) or any value not larger than the segment's size.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success the shared memory segment identifier (a non-negative integer) is
returned.  On error \-1 is returned and
.I errno
is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EACCES
A segment exists for
.I key
but the caller lacks permission.
.TP
.B EEXIST
.B IPC_CREAT
and
.B IPC_EXCL
were set and a segment already exists for
.IR key .
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I size
is less than
.B SHMMIN
or greater than
.BR SHMMAX ,
or a segment exists for
.I key
but is smaller than the requested
.IR size .
.TP
.B ENOENT
No segment exists for
.I key
and
.B IPC_CREAT
was not set.
.TP
.B ENOSPC
The system-wide limit on shared memory segments
.RB ( SHMMNI )
would be exceeded.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Insufficient contiguous physical memory to create the segment.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shmat (2),
.BR shmdt (2),
.BR shmctl (2),
.BR ftok (3)
